  "InputApiHint": "Legacy DirectInput (dinput.dll). A Windows 11 crash report shows Cricket07.exe crashing inside DINPUT.dll - see the Controllers tab (unplug HID devices / dinputto8).",
  "Notes": "Direct3D 8, 4:3 game. Known on Windows 10/11: crash on start (one report: worked on Windows 10, crashes on Windows 11), crash inside DINPUT.dll while enumerating input devices, and limited resolutions. Resolution is stored as two little-endian 16-bit values in the binary .pro profile in Documents\\EA SPORTS(TM) Cricket 07 - the Game config tab can edit it (backup first). Widescreen needs a community mod (e.g. retrobone/EACricketWidescreenFix), which you install yourself.",
  "DrmNotes": "Retail disc uses SafeDisc 4 (PCGamingWiki, GameCopyWorld; the browser-port project also states the retail Cricket07.exe is SafeDisc-wrapped). SafeDisc's secdrv.sys driver is disabled on Windows 10/11, so the disc check cannot run there. No official DRM-free or digital re-release is known. This launcher only reports SafeDisc - it never removes or bypasses it.",
